WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.815 --> 00:00:08.516
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WELL MIKE ROWE HAS

00:00:08.517 --> 00:00:10.284
LONG BEEN A CHAMPION OF

00:00:10.285 --> 00:00:11.719
DIGNIFIED OLD FASHION LABOR, THE

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.087
KIND WHERE YOU GET DIRTY.

00:00:13.088 --> 00:00:16.123
BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN HE IS

00:00:16.124 --> 00:00:18.259
CLOSE-MINDED OR ADVERSE TO

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:18.659
TECHNOLOGY.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.693
HIS NEW SHOW "RETURNING THE

00:00:19.694 --> 00:00:21.095
FAVOR" IS ONE OF THE BIGGEST

00:00:21.096 --> 00:00:23.531
THINGS ON FACEBOOK.

00:00:23.532 --> 00:00:23.998
IMPRESSIVE.

00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:25.866
TALENT RUNS IN HIS FAMILY.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:27.501
MIKE'S MOTHER PEGGY HAS A BRAND

00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:29.036
NEW BOOK COMING OUT TOMORROW

00:00:29.037 --> 00:00:30.271
CALLED "ABOUT MY MOTHER."

00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:32.540
TRUE STORIES OF A HORSE CRAZY

00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:33.774
DAUGHTER AND HER BASEBALL

00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:35.576
OBSESSED MOTHER.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.244
MIKE AND PEGGY JOIN US TONIGHT.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:39.180
WE ARE GRATEFUL THEY ARE HERE.

00:00:39.181 --> 00:00:42.116
PEGGY, AS YOU KNOW, YOUR SON IS

00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:45.786
AN FOLK HERO ON THIS SHOW.

00:00:45.787 --> 00:00:47.555
BELOVED BY OUR VIEWERS.

00:00:47.556 --> 00:00:49.990
&gt;&gt; YOU MADE IT WEIRD, TUCKER.

00:00:49.991 --> 00:00:52.026
YOU MADE IT WEIRD!

00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:52.426
[ LAUGHTER ]

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:55.563
&gt;&gt; YOU DIDN'T TELL ME IT WAS

00:00:55.564 --> 00:00:57.832
THAT KIND OF SHOW.

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:59.400
&gt;&gt; SHE RATED IT JUST LIKE THAT.

00:00:59.401 --> 00:01:01.068
&gt;&gt; Tucker: I CAN SEE HE IS YOUR

00:01:01.069 --> 00:01:01.468
SON.

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:02.870
I'M SO IMPRESSED.

00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:04.972
WHAT WAS HE LIKE WHEN HE WAS

00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:05.306
YOUNGER?

00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:07.775
&gt;&gt; YOU WON'T BELIEVE IT, BUT HE

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:08.409
WAS VERY SHY.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.476
&gt;&gt; Tucker: REALLY?

00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:09.977
&gt;&gt; HE WAS.

00:01:09.978 --> 00:01:11.812
HE WAS -- IN FACT, WHEN SOMEBODY

00:01:11.813 --> 00:01:14.148
WOULD COME TO THE FRONT DOOR

00:01:14.149 --> 00:01:15.216
SOMETIMES, HE WOULD JUST DIVE

00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:18.619
UNDER THE KITCHEN TABLE OR INTO

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.087
THE HALL CLOSET.

00:01:20.088 --> 00:01:21.155
AND HE WAS A NEAT FREAK.

00:01:21.156 --> 00:01:24.024
HE DIDN'T WANT TO GET DIRTY.

00:01:24.025 --> 00:01:25.259
&gt;&gt; Tucker: I WAS GONNA ASK YOU

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.894
WHAT'S THE MOST EMBARRASSING

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:28.495
THING, BUT I THINK YOU TOLD US.

00:01:28.496 --> 00:01:30.197
HE DOVE INTO THE HALL CLOSET.

00:01:30.198 --> 00:01:31.432
HOW DID YOU GET HIM OUT?

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:34.969
&gt;&gt; WHEN THE PEOPLE LEFT, HE CAME

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:35.236
OUT.

00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:36.070
&gt;&gt; GREAT.

00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:37.638
HEADLINE TOMORROW, MIKE ROWE'S

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.240
MOM EXPLAINS HOW HE CAME OUT OF

00:01:39.241 --> 00:01:40.207
THE CLOSET.

00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:42.676
THANKS, TUCKER.

00:01:42.677 --> 00:01:43.878
AWESOME JOB.

00:01:43.879 --> 00:01:44.278
[ LAUGHTER ]

00:01:44.279 --> 00:01:45.746
&gt;&gt; Tucker: I KNEW I COULD GET

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:46.013
IT.

00:01:46.014 --> 00:01:47.381
MY SKILL AS AN INTERVIEWER.

00:01:47.382 --> 00:01:48.916
IS THAT STORY IN THE BOOK,

00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:50.117
MRS. ROWE?

00:01:50.118 --> 00:01:52.786
&gt;&gt; NOT IN THIS BOOK, BUT IT'S IN

00:01:52.787 --> 00:01:54.788
MY NEXT BOOK.

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:55.522
&gt;&gt; POPUP.

00:01:55.523 --> 00:01:56.624
&gt;&gt; Tucker: A POPUP.

00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:58.525
HAVE YOU READ THIS BOOK, MIKE?

00:01:58.526 --> 00:01:59.326
&gt;&gt; READ IT?

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:00.628
I WROTE THE FORWARD TO IT.

00:02:00.629 --> 00:02:01.962
DO YOU KNOW WHAT MAKES YOU

00:02:01.963 --> 00:02:02.296
AWESOME?

00:02:02.297 --> 00:02:03.731
LAST TIME I WAS ON YOUR SHOW, WE

00:02:03.732 --> 00:02:05.065
WERE TALKING ABOUT GOOD NEWS AND

00:02:05.066 --> 00:02:06.901
I SAID, NEXT TIME I'M BRINGING

00:02:06.902 --> 00:02:08.602
MY MOTHER AND YOU SAID, GO

00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:09.970
AHEAD, AND YOU MEANT IT.

00:02:09.971 --> 00:02:11.672
SO I'M SITTING HERE WITH MY

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:13.574
MOTHER BECAUSE SHE'S WRITEN THE

00:02:13.575 --> 00:02:14.942
ULTIMATE BOOK OF GOOD NEWS.

00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:17.111
THIS IS -- SHE'S BEEN WRITING ME

00:02:17.112 --> 00:02:17.778
STORIES FOR YEAR.

00:02:17.779 --> 00:02:19.613
I STARTED READING THEM ON

00:02:19.614 --> 00:02:20.681
FACEBOOK.

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:21.582
PUBLISHERS FELL IN LOVE WITH

00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:23.017
THEM AND A BOOK POPPED OUT.

00:02:23.018 --> 00:02:27.221
THIS IS A BOOK, 19 STORIES ABOUT

00:02:27.222 --> 00:02:28.422
GROWING UP NEXT TO HER MOTHER,

00:02:28.423 --> 00:02:29.623
MY NANA.

00:02:29.624 --> 00:02:31.191
THE TWO OF THEM ABSOLUTELY

00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:33.160
NOTHING IN COMMON, LOVED EACH

00:02:33.161 --> 00:02:35.729
OTHER DEARLY FOR 70 YEARS.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.198
THIS BOOK IN THESE TIMES, IN MY

00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:40.901
HUMBLE ESTIMATION, TUCKER -- I

00:02:40.902 --> 00:02:44.438
DON'T WANT OVERSTATE IT.

00:02:44.439 --> 00:02:47.508
THIS IS THE BALM OUR COUNTRY

00:02:47.509 --> 00:02:47.808
NEEDS.

00:02:47.809 --> 00:02:49.576
&gt;&gt; Tucker: B-A-L-M.

00:02:49.577 --> 00:02:51.578
I ABSOLUTELY BELIEVE THAT.

00:02:51.579 --> 00:02:53.080
I'M SINCERE.

00:02:53.081 --> 00:02:56.650
THIS IS EXACTLY WHAT WE NEED.

00:02:56.651 --> 00:02:59.353
I WOULD SAY ALL OF OUR VIEWERS,

00:02:59.354 --> 00:03:01.522
NO MATTER WHO THEY VOTED FOR,

00:03:01.523 --> 00:03:03.824
WHAT THEY THINK, WHO THEY PRAY

00:03:03.825 --> 00:03:05.759
TO ARE FANS OF YOURS AND YOUR

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.060
MOM'S.

00:03:06.061 --> 00:03:07.828
HOW LONG DID IT TAKE TO WRITE

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:09.563
THIS, MRS. ROWE?

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:11.565
&gt;&gt;IVE WRITING IT FOR YEARS,

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:11.932
ACTUALLY.

00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:13.200
I HAVE WRITTEN SEVERAL STORIES

00:03:13.201 --> 00:03:14.401
OVER THE YEARS AND PUBLISHED

00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:16.003
THEM IN NEWSPAPERS AND

00:03:16.004 --> 00:03:16.370
MAGAZINES.

00:03:16.371 --> 00:03:18.572
AND THE RESPONSE WAS SO

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:18.939
POSITIVE.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.442
PEOPLE LOVED A FEEL-GOOD STORY.

00:03:21.443 --> 00:03:22.409
AND THEY'RE TRUE.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.778
AND SO I DECIDED TO WRITE SOME

00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:26.947
MORE AND PUT THEM TOGETHER IN A

00:03:26.948 --> 00:03:27.247
BOOK.

00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:28.849
&gt;&gt; DO YOU WANT THE TRUE STORY,

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:29.183
TUCKER?

00:03:29.184 --> 00:03:29.650
&gt;&gt; Tucker: YES.

00:03:29.651 --> 00:03:31.418
&gt;&gt; SHE COMES HOME FROM MACY'S

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:33.020
ONE DAY AND SAYS, YOU'LL NEVER

00:03:33.021 --> 00:03:34.722
BELIEVE WHAT NANA DID.

00:03:34.723 --> 00:03:36.657
SHE SAID, I WAS PUSHING HER IN

00:03:36.658 --> 00:03:38.492
THE WHEELCHAIR AND SHE SAW AN

00:03:38.493 --> 00:03:38.993
ORIOLES JERSEY.

00:03:38.994 --> 00:03:41.695
SHE LEAPS OUT OF HER WHEELCHAIR,

00:03:41.696 --> 00:03:43.430
TAKES OFF HER BLOUSE, PUTS ON

00:03:43.431 --> 00:03:44.598
THE ORIOLES JERSEY.

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:46.333
MY MOTHER HAS A HEART ATTACK

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:48.569
SAYS, MOM, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.937
NANA SAYS, NOBODY CARES.

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.739
I'M AN OLD WOMAN IN A BRA.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:52.039
RIGHT?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.574
THEN KNOCKS THE MANNEQUIN OVER.

00:03:53.575 --> 00:03:55.943
HEAD FALLS OFF, ROLLS DOWN THE

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:56.243
AISLE.

00:03:56.244 --> 00:03:57.444
PEOPLE START SCATTERING.

00:03:57.445 --> 00:03:59.046
MOM COMES HOME AND SAYS,

00:03:59.047 --> 00:04:00.481
MICHAEL, I THINK THE TIME HAS

00:04:00.482 --> 00:04:02.583
COME TO WRITE A BOOK ABOUT YOUR

00:04:02.584 --> 00:04:02.983
GRANDMOTHER.

00:04:02.984 --> 00:04:04.385
&gt;&gt; Tucker: NANA WAS NOT HIDING

00:04:04.386 --> 00:04:07.755
IN THE HALL CLOSET WHEN PEOPLE

00:04:07.756 --> 00:04:10.290
CAME OVER.

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:11.759
SHE WAS SELF-CONFIDENT.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.627
&gt;&gt; IT SOUNDS UNBELIEVABLE, BUT

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:15.496
EVERY WORD WAS TRUE THAT HE JUST

00:04:15.497 --> 00:04:15.896
SAID.

00:04:15.897 --> 00:04:16.897
&gt;&gt; Tucker: BY THE WAY,

00:04:16.898 --> 00:04:19.166
EVERYTHING THE ROWE FAMILY TELLS

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:20.401
US, WE TAKE ATE FACE VALUE.

00:04:20.402 --> 00:04:21.602
YOU ARE THE MOST BELIEVABLE

00:04:21.603 --> 00:04:22.369
PEOPLE WE KNOW.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:25.039
I HOPE YOU'LL BOTH COME BACK.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.240
CONGRATULATIONS ON THE BOOK.

00:04:26.241 --> 00:04:27.241
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU.

00:04:27.242 --> 00:04:31.178
&gt;&gt; BY TWAY, ONE GOOD TURN

00:04:31.179 --> 00:04:31.779
DESERVES ANOTHER.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.547
MOM STARTED A NEW BOOK TODAY

00:04:33.548 --> 00:04:36.484
"SHIP OF FOOLS."

